     The aforementioned analysis technique may allow the organization to conduct more efficient and meaningful assessments (in the sense that the assessment technique may be better able to identify those individuals who will perform better in a given position based on the performance metric). Consequently, a manager or a supervisor of a prospective employee in the organization and/or a representative of human resources for the organization can use the analysis technique to improve the hiring practices of the organization. In this way, the analysis technique may help the organization improve its human capital in a targeted manner (specific to a particular position or job type in the organization), which may help the organization compete and succeed in the marketplace. 
