         FIG. 21A  provides a schematic view of defining a second level region of magnification on a first level image,  FIG. 21B  illustrates selecting in real time a first “snapshot” of the first level image at the second level of magnification, which first “snapshot” remains overlaid on the first level image,  FIG. 21C  illustrates selecting (e.g., in real time) a second “snapshot” of the first level image at the second level of magnification, which second “snapshot” remains overlaid on the first level image, and  FIG. 21D  provides an alternative view in which the user has created a second level image that encompasses the entirety of the object of interest shown in  FIG. 21A ; 
